                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1cb00db8-5c6b-3d46-8503-9c525dfb49a9",
                        "entry_id": "183716af-95cb-3403-bddd-535200c680f4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "kleine Figuren, häufig aus Porzellan oder Glas; Ziergegenstände"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "940bf896-cf7d-40d2-a12b-2a707179bf6f",
                                "sense_id": "1cb00db8-5c6b-3d46-8503-9c525dfb49a9",
                                "text": "Die ganze Wohnung von Oma stand voll mit Nippes!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "752966cc-3e37-4d23-a34d-392c48a1b0c9",
                                "sense_id": "1cb00db8-5c6b-3d46-8503-9c525dfb49a9",
                                "text": "„Val staubte den Nippes ab, wischte über die Fensterbank.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af0724f0-6729-455f-a47c-5d059ad1e680",
                                "sense_id": "1cb00db8-5c6b-3d46-8503-9c525dfb49a9",
                                "text": "„Er besaß große bauchige Gläser mit hohen Stielen, und Kristensa erschien es gekünstelt, Wein aus solchem Nippes zu trinken.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "01bac460-4ecd-4cdd-a5e9-6819a5860f3d",
                        "source_entry_id": "183716af-95cb-3403-bddd-535200c680f4",
                        "source_sense_id": "1cb00db8-5c6b-3d46-8503-9c525dfb49a9",
                        "source_sense_description": "kleine Figuren, häufig aus Porzellan oder Glas; Ziergegenstände",
                        "target_lang_word": "knick-knack",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "knick-knack",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab9e0d3f-8b75-3e64-adbb-6ce638052d87",
                                        "entry_id": "70cb0a95-897c-3870-96cc-460fc142818d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small ornament or other object of minor value."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aef9f990-1779-4469-a42e-b537554bf948",
                                                "sense_id": "ab9e0d3f-8b75-3e64-adbb-6ce638052d87",
                                                "text": "Our Cutler, who had now a great Stock of things of his Handy-work, gave them some little Knick Knacks, as Plates of Silver and of Iron, cut Diamond Fashion, and cut into Hearts and into Rings, and they were mightily pleased."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a7e310c-253c-4f99-8c92-30bace7350c8",
                                                "sense_id": "ab9e0d3f-8b75-3e64-adbb-6ce638052d87",
                                                "text": "But there was no hitch in the conversation, nevertheless; for one gentleman, who travelled in the perfumery line, exhibited an interesting nick-nack, in the way of a remarkable cake of shaving soap, which he had lately met with in Germany […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec26070e-beb4-4211-afde-fbe4158dc304",
                                                "sense_id": "ab9e0d3f-8b75-3e64-adbb-6ce638052d87",
                                                "text": "The room was small, and densely filled with furniture; it gave an impression of faded silk and little statuettes which might totter if one moved. Rosier got up and wandered about with his careful tread, bending over the tables charged with knick-knacks and the cushions embossed with princely arms."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb3d51e6-7f50-4543-9fcd-4f47bd7bb019",
                                                "sense_id": "ab9e0d3f-8b75-3e64-adbb-6ce638052d87",
                                                "text": "Is art anything that we have reason to value? Or is it a mere adornment of life which we can do without—a mere knick-knack for Dame Civilization to hang about her wrinkled neck in order to dazzle her neighbours?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd010347-9aa9-49e5-a6b6-974bb6496d1e",
                                                "sense_id": "ab9e0d3f-8b75-3e64-adbb-6ce638052d87",
                                                "text": "1985, Herbert Kretzmer, \"Master of the House\" (song) in Les Misérables\nPicking up their knick-knacks when they can't see straight"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "34adfd53-58ca-4b31-a772-1aaa4675910c",
                        "source_entry_id": "183716af-95cb-3403-bddd-535200c680f4",
                        "source_sense_id": "1cb00db8-5c6b-3d46-8503-9c525dfb49a9",
                        "source_sense_description": "kleine Figuren, häufig aus Porzellan oder Glas; Ziergegenstände",
                        "target_lang_word": "knickknackery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "knickknackery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c5862db-5956-371e-b704-debcb2888ed9",
                                        "entry_id": "1c7a8e45-1771-375b-8975-f7e91cf36749",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Various trinkets or novelties; bric-a-brac."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43b7148d-d099-483e-92ca-338df04049f8",
                                                "sense_id": "1c5862db-5956-371e-b704-debcb2888ed9",
                                                "text": "As Hortense says of the gilded knicknackery of her saloon,—\n\"Est-ce utile?\nC'est plus, c'est nécessaire.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7243d5fb-acb9-428c-9756-e43ed979449f",
                        "source_entry_id": "183716af-95cb-3403-bddd-535200c680f4",
                        "source_sense_id": "1cb00db8-5c6b-3d46-8503-9c525dfb49a9",
                        "source_sense_description": "kleine Figuren, häufig aus Porzellan oder Glas; Ziergegenstände",
                        "target_lang_word": "bibelot",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bibelot",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f24dd075-15b9-36a1-89b0-ac434f522ca4",
                                        "entry_id": "f98957c5-f60a-38c1-9d35-f8bf76e76d04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Petit objet décoratif, souvent fait de verre ou de porcelaine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "014a3446-a3e5-4062-b8cf-271323f88629",
                                                "sense_id": "f24dd075-15b9-36a1-89b0-ac434f522ca4",
                                                "text": "Le bibelot encore, et encore le bibelot dans les brasseries d’étudiants où le fils du bourgeois de province accoude sa flânerie sur une table de style, devant un verre de façon ancienne, sous une lumière tamisée par des vitraux coloriés."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b90b135b-48bd-4764-9f05-8c0ea355e3a0",
                                                "sense_id": "f24dd075-15b9-36a1-89b0-ac434f522ca4",
                                                "text": "Je me borne à signaler les lévriers anglais, écossais, russes, les bull-dogs ; puis les chiens d’appartement, havanais, carlins, et ces délicieux terriers du Yorkshire qui atteignent au rang de véritables bibelots."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06405552-6fab-4025-bd51-e2aed4cddf8a",
                                                "sense_id": "f24dd075-15b9-36a1-89b0-ac434f522ca4",
                                                "text": "Car enfin, n'est-ce pas là, dans ce cimetière des vanités, entre cartes postales et bibelots que s'achève irrémédiablement toute comédie littéraire ?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
